  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-02-17T04:22:38.188Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, in its basic form, VRChat has many functions that require you to first bring up your VR Hand Menu before you can select certain actions, like emoting, emojis or even toggeling game options like Muting yourself. While it is true most users do not play with a keyboard, or gamepad, many do, and being able to map controls to the following features would be greatly welcome. Quick access to these actions would improve the quality of life for most end users. Simply default these to no keybind and allow users to set their own.\n- Emotes 1-8\n- Emojis 1-6\n- Toggle sit and stand mode\n- Mute/Unmute yourself (for anyone who has mic always on selected.)\n- Changing of the Push to talk key.\n- Toggle Personal Space mode\n- Toggle Mute all other users on and off, (for quick relief of a sound you cant find source of)",
